Vendored from rustmigemo 0.1.7-dev.0, commit
121101dfcfd9465c998ba53fabe43773b14bf868:
https://github.com/oguna/rustmigemo

The MIT license and upstream third-party notices are retained alongside the
runtime source. The optional CLI and examples are omitted; the manifest has
its bin target removed and automatic bin discovery disabled.

Local fixes: LoudsTrie::first_child treats the end of the bit vector as a leaf,
and BitVector::rank handles prefixes ending at a 64-bit word boundary at the
end of the vector, including 512-bit rank-block boundaries and the empty
vector. These fixes prevent panics on valid small dictionaries. Run the
boundary regressions from the Nucleo checkout with
`cargo test --test rustmigemo-boundaries`.
